# SPA fallback for Apache/LiteSpeed-style static hosting.
#
# The live host (scrollhaus.website) answers every request directly —
# including 404s — with headers reading `platform: hostinger`, `Server: hcdn`,
# not Netlify's edge. That means netlify.toml's own catch-all redirect (which
# IS correct, and stays in the repo in case the pipeline ever changes) has no
# effect on the domain that's actually live. Confirmed empirically: a direct
# hit on /templates 404s with Hostinger's own branded error page, while the
# root path and every in-app client-side navigation (history.pushState, no
# server round-trip) both work fine — this rule only matters for a hard
# load/refresh/bookmark of a non-root path.
#
# Rewrite anything that isn't a real file or directory on disk to index.html,
# so React's own routing (see App.tsx's VIEW_PATH/viewFromPath) takes over
# client-side exactly as it does when you arrive via a nav click instead.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On
  RewriteBase /
  RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} -f [OR]
  RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} -d
  RewriteRule ^ - [L]
  RewriteRule ^ index.html [L]
</IfModule>
